📦 Batch Normalization
Batch normalization normalizes the inputs to each layer across the mini-batch. Benefits include:

Faster training

Reduced sensitivity to initialization

Acts as a regularizer

It’s often applied between the linear transformation and the activation.
BATCH NORMALIZATION
-Center around zero  and normalize  inputs of each layer in the network. than inputs are scaled and an offest is added.
-Achieves the same accuracy of a network that doesn't  use this technique  faster.
-can lead to better performance
-It doesn't need a standardization layer
-reduces the need for other regularization
-epochs take longer due to the amount of computations but convergence will be faster.

