🧪 Key Hyperparameters to Tune
To train effectively, you'll need to configure:

Learning rate: Controls how fast weights update

-Batch size: Number of samples per gradient update.
It helps with generalization, because the entire batch is not fed at once into the model.


-Number of iterations/ Epochs: Number of passes through the entire dataset.
You can choose how many times to feed the dataset to the model, the more iterations you make, higher the probability 
that the model will overfit. Early stopping can be used.

Number of layers & neurons: Model architecture

Activation functions

Weight initialization

Regularization strength (L1, L2). It makes the network simpler. We use it to deal with overfitting.


Dropout rate

Optimizer settings (e.g., momentum, β1/β2 in Adam)

